{"path":"docs/concepts/overview/components/index.html","title":"Kubernetes Components","description":"This page provides a high-level overview of the essential components that make up a Kubernetes cluster.","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Kubernetes Components"}]},{"type":"text","value":"An overview of the key components that make up a Kubernetes cluster."},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This page provides a high-level overview of the essential components that make up a Kubernetes cluster."}]},{"type":"image","src":"assets/78f007894bfc5d0eed047777da3ea0f6f8b15e5d656ef24b21675b3ffae3bb5e.svg","alt":"Components of Kubernetes"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The components of a Kubernetes cluster"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"core-components","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Core Components"},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/overview/components/index.html#core-components","title":null,"children":[]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A Kubernetes cluster consists of a control plane and one or more worker nodes. Here's a brief overview of the main components:"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":"control-plane-components","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Control Plane Components"},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/overview/components/index.html#control-plane-components","title":null,"children":[]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Manage the overall state of the cluster:"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/architecture/index.html#kube-apiserver","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"kube-apiserver"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"The core component server that exposes the Kubernetes HTTP API."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/architecture/index.html#etcd","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"etcd"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Consistent and highly-available key value store for all API server data."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/architecture/index.html#kube-scheduler","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"kube-scheduler"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Looks for Pods not yet bound to a node, and assigns each Pod to a suitable node."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/architecture/index.html#kube-controller-manager","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"kube-controller-manager"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Runs "},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/architecture/controller/index.html","title":"A control loop that watches the shared state of the cluster through the apiserver and makes changes attempting to move the current state towards the desired state.","children":[{"type":"text","value":"controllers"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to implement Kubernetes API behavior."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/architecture/index.html#cloud-controller-manager","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"cloud-controller-manager"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (optional)"}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Integrates with underlying cloud provider(s)."}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":"node-components","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Node Components"},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/overview/components/index.html#node-components","title":null,"children":[]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run on every node, maintaining running pods and providing the Kubernetes runtime environment:"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/architecture/index.html#kubelet","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"kubelet"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Ensures that Pods are running, including their containers."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/architecture/index.html#kube-proxy","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"kube-proxy"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (optional)"}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Maintains network rules on nodes to implement "},{"type":"link","href":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/services-networking/service/","title":"A way to expose an application running on a set of Pods as a network service.","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Services"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/architecture/index.html#container-runtime","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Container runtime"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Software responsible for running containers. Read "},{"type":"link","href":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/setup/production-environment/container-runtimes/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Container Runtimes"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to learn more."}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"🛇 This item links to a third party project or product that is not part of Kubernetes itself. "},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/overview/components/index.html#third-party-content-disclaimer","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"More information"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your cluster may require additional software on each node; for example, you might also run "},{"type":"link","href":"https://systemd.io/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"systemd"}]},{"type":"text","value":" on a Linux node to supervise local components."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"addons","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Addons"},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/overview/components/index.html#addons","title":null,"children":[]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Addons extend the functionality of Kubernetes. A few important examples include:"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/architecture/index.html#dns","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"DNS"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"For cluster-wide DNS resolution."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/architecture/index.html#web-ui-dashboard","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Web UI"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (Dashboard)"}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"For cluster management via a web interface."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/architecture/index.html#container-resource-monitoring","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Container Resource Monitoring"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"For collecting and storing container metrics."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/architecture/index.html#cluster-level-logging","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cluster-level Logging"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"For saving container logs to a central log store."}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"flexibility-in-architecture","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Flexibility in Architecture"},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/overview/components/index.html#flexibility-in-architecture","title":null,"children":[]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Kubernetes allows for flexibility in how these components are deployed and managed. The architecture can be adapted to various needs, from small development environments to large-scale production deployments."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For more detailed information about each component and various ways to configure your cluster architecture, see the "},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/architecture/index.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cluster Architecture"}]},{"type":"text","value":" page."}]},{"type":"anchor","id":"third-party-content-discl